  "body": "## What changed\n`crates/sim/src/verify/tilt_span.rs`: `in_cap` now accepts A/B letters at exactly +-90 degrees (`<= 90`, was `< 90`). A span that stays inside the closed cap reads no span floor. Letters past 90 still get #1303's interval floor. The module's law and the decision are written out in `docs/decisions/1404-closed-tilt-cap.md`.\n\n## Culprit\nPR #1306 (merge `e74bca1f9`, #1303 tilt-band dip). Release lane bisect: v0.18.0 green, `a0d102834` green, `e74bca1f9` red, current main red.\n\n## Which side was wrong: the check\nAll 18 hits are blade-lying swarf links that turn B +90 -> -90 with A = C = 0. In the span from the sampled pose B 45 to its neighbour at exactly B 90, the strict cap fell back to the interval bound (`sin_max = 1`), which gives the floor `tip - R`. The turn cells pinned that floor over B 45's footprint, where the band really stands about 34 mm above the tip. Instrumented reading: cell bottoms -3.7 to -5.5 over columns 47 mm out, with the stock top at 9.6 to 11.7.\n\nThe dip that floor describes belongs to the horizontal end, and that end's own cells read it in place. On the closed cap, cos A and cos B are >= 0 along the lerp and `ln cos A + ln cos B` is concave, so `cos θ` is smallest at an end (by continuity also where it is 0 there). The ends therefore bound the span. The generator's contact was not real: the cells that follow the actual band positions find nothing once the misplaced floor is gone.\n\n## Readings / tests\n- `cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test operations -- --ignored swarf`: both full-band tests pass (they were red on main with 18 SweepHits).\n- New pin `verify::sweep::tests::a_swing_through_vertical_reads_no_floor_from_its_horizontal_ends`: checks no span floor at any pose, a post 47 mm out topped at +10 is clean, one topped at +40 is still refused, and one under a horizontal end's band (70 mm out, top -2) is still refused. It fails on the strict cap.\n- Extended `verify::tilt_span::tests::inside_the_cap_the_samples_bound_the_span_and_past_it_the_floor_does`: 400 brute-force spans with ends at exactly +-90 read `None`, and the lerp never stands under the samples. It fails on the strict cap.\n- #1303's pins are unchanged and green (`a_span_past_a_right_angle_...`, `the_backstop_reads_the_exact_dip_lowered_by_the_span_floor`, `tilt_band_dip`, `tilt_tolerance`, `midturn_swept_band`, `midturn_hidden_backstop`).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green (sim 35 s, motion 10 s, app 482 s). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nThe rest of the release tier (other heavy lanes, UI snapshots) was not run. That is for the cut.\n\nChangelog: The mid-turn sweep no longer refuses a blade-lying swarf link that turns B through vertical: a horizontal end's dip is no longer pinned onto the in-between poses (#1404)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1404\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
